    "detailed_description": "Ad Victoriam is an indie game with a simple premise: &quot;what would it have felt like to be on an ancient battlefield and observe the clash of armies unfolding?&quot;<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUsing parallel computing, Ad Victoriam can simulate tens of thousands of soldiers all displayed in real time! Soldiers will maneuver together and fight in groups - at least that is, until the heat of battle causes them to break ranks and flee. We've put great emphasis on realism and immersion - soldiers neither mob as mindless zombies nor fight in perfect unison as permanent unit blocks.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe year is 59 BC. You, Julius Caesar, have become a Consul. It is time to seek fortune in conquest. New lands await, and perhaps one day Rome itself! To victory! Ad victoriam!",
    "about_the_game": "Ad Victoriam is an indie game with a simple premise: &quot;what would it have felt like to be on an ancient battlefield and observe the clash of armies unfolding?&quot;<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUsing parallel computing, Ad Victoriam can simulate tens of thousands of soldiers all displayed in real time! Soldiers will maneuver together and fight in groups - at least that is, until the heat of battle causes them to break ranks and flee. We've put great emphasis on realism and immersion - soldiers neither mob as mindless zombies nor fight in perfect unison as permanent unit blocks.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe year is 59 BC. You, Julius Caesar, have become a Consul. It is time to seek fortune in conquest. New lands await, and perhaps one day Rome itself! To victory! Ad victoriam!",
    "short_description": "Ad Victoriam lets you experience large scale immersive battles and lead Caesar's legions to victory in a groundbreaking simulator! You can start up custom battles or play a full strategy game as you conquer Gaul and establish the Roman Empire!",
    "supported_languages": "English",
